{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaCKRecursionKernelConstraints","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaCKRecursionKernelConstraints","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaReebSinhParity"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bridge_cannot_reach_c3_target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bridge_cannot_reach_c3_target","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCKRecursionKernelConstraints.lean#L132-L140","doc":"**C13 refutation — the `Δtr_M`-seeded linear bridge cannot produce\n`c₃ = -2`.** If both principled seedings reached `-2` at a single `b`, then\n`b = 50/77` and `b = 175/288` simultaneously — impossible. Hence the mode→ladder\n`f` is non-linear in `Δtr_M` (refuted-class map row C13, PR #2465). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bridge_c3_seedings_inconsistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bridge_c3_seedings_inconsistent","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCKRecursionKernelConstraints.lean#L127-L130","doc":"**C13 inconsistency — the two seedings need different `b`.** `50/77 ≠\n175/288`, so the raw and bar-even seedings cannot both reach `-2` at one `b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bridge_c3_bareven_requires_b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bridge_c3_bareven_requires_b","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCKRecursionKernelConstraints.lean#L120-L125","doc":"**C13 (#1602 bar-even seeding) — the bridge `c₃ = -175/(144 b)` hits `-2`\nonly at `b = 175/288`.** Same bridge with the bar-even projection of `Δtr_M`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.bridge_c3_raw_requires_b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.bridge_c3_raw_requires_b","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCKRecursionKernelConstraints.lean#L111-L118","doc":"**C13 (raw seeding) — the bridge `c₃ = -100/(77 b)` hits `-2` only at\n`b = 50/77`.** The #1622 mode→ladder bridge seeded by the raw even-in-ℏ part of\n`Δtr_M`, scale-fixed to `c₂ = -1`, yields `c₃ = -100/(77 b)` (PR #2465 witness).\nForcing it to the `J_Hopf(1) = -2` target pins `b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ck_a1_bar_odd_of_c3_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ck_a1_bar_odd_of_c3_odd","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCKRecursionKernelConstraints.lean#L88-L109","doc":"**Kernel leading coefficient is bar-ODD — CONDITIONAL on the exactly-odd\nhypothesis `hodd`.** Since `a₁ = -c₃` pointwise in the substrate angle `η`,\n*if* `c₃` is bar-antisymmetric (`c₃(-η) = -c₃(η)`) then `a₁` is bar-odd.\n\nScope clarification (2026-07-07 investigation,\n`docs/audits/2026-07-07-a1-bar-odd-parity-shadow-investigation.md`): the\nantecedent `hodd` is a modelling hypothesis from the #1887 swing narrative,\nproved nowhere — #1887's Lean establishes component parity (`sinh` bar-odd,\nand the bar-antisymmetric *part* of a Reeb holonomy is its `sinh` component),\nnot pointwise oddness of `c₃`. An *exactly* bar-odd `a₁` would moreover have\nzero q=1 shadow (`QOU.QBeta.fixed_eval_two_mul_kills_bar_odd`), contradicting\nthe §4(c) gate `c₃ → -2`. Established reading: `a₁` has a nonzero bar-ODD\npart (the anchor-swing channel); its bar-even part carries the shadow.\n\nRenamed 2026-07-07: `ck_a1_bar_odd` → `ck_a1_bar_odd_of_c3_odd` (the `_of_`\nnaming rule for hypothesis-carrying constraint lemmas — the antecedent is\nnow visible in every citation; see `local/formalizer.md` §Conditional-lemma\nnaming). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ck_c4_constant_depth_two_prediction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ck_c4_constant_depth_two_prediction","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCKRecursionKernelConstraints.lean#L79-L86","doc":"**Constant depth-2 kernel predicts `c₄ = 1 - c₃²`.** Constraints `a₂ = -1`\nand `a₁ = -c₃` fully determine a *constant* depth-2 kernel; the `n = 4` rung\n`f_4 = a₁·f_3 + a₂·f_2 = (-c₃)·c₃ + (-1)·(-1)` then forces `c₄ = 1 - c₃²`. The\ncompanion probe shows this misses the fitted `c₄ ≈ -0.972` by ~3.4× at both\nanchors ⇒ the recursion is depth ≥ 3 or non-constant (Habiro `(u;u)_m` basis). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ck_a1_eq_sqrt2_phi2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ck_a1_eq_sqrt2_phi2","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCKRecursionKernelConstraints.lean#L70-L77","doc":"**The kernel's leading coefficient is the #1887 Φ₂ (up to √2).** Combining\n`a₁ = -c₃` with the #1887 phase relation `c₃ = -(Φ₁·Φ₂)` and `Φ₁ = √2`:\n`a₁ = √2·Φ₂`. The kernel's leading coefficient and the open Φ₂ are the same\nobject. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ck_a1_eq_neg_c3_depth_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ck_a1_eq_neg_c3_depth_two","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCKRecursionKernelConstraints.lean#L63-L68","doc":"**Depth-2 leading coefficient pinned: `a₁ = -c₃`.** At the `n = 3` rung\n`f_3 = a₁·f_2 + a₂·f_1` with `f_2 = -1`, `f_1 = 0`, so `c₃ = -a₁` regardless of\n`a₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ck_a2_eq_c2_depth_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ck_a2_eq_c2_depth_two","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCKRecursionKernelConstraints.lean#L57-L61","doc":"**Depth-2 second coefficient pinned: `a₂ = c₂` (`= -1`).** At the `n = 2`\nrung `f_2 = a₁·f_1 + a₂·f_0` with `f_1 = 0`, `f_0 = 1`, so `c₂ = a₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.ck_recursion_depth_one_refuted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.ck_recursion_depth_one_refuted","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCKRecursionKernelConstraints.lean#L51-L55","doc":"**Depth-1 kernel refuted.** A depth-1 recursion gives `f_2 = a₁·f_1`; with\nthe ladder seed `f_1 = 0` this is `0`, contradicting the proved `f_2 = c_2 = -1`.\nSo the c_k-recursion kernel has depth ≥ 2. ","signatureChunk":0}]}